; Verdict 131071 — seventeen readings:
;   three of the four languages have a real toolchain                     1
;   and ONE does not — Form, reported UNJUDGED rather than passed,
;     because an unrun language scoring like a passing one is the
;     blindness this cell exists to end                                   2
;   every judged language matches the graph, case for case                4
;   python: a page emitted, run by python3, every answer compared         8
;   javascript: emitted, run by node                                     16
;   go: emitted, compiled and run by go                                  32
;   Form has no runner row and is honest about it                        64
;
;   THE SWEEP, sized from the graph rather than from a typed number:
;   more than 100 cases — every (shape, relation, key) triple some
;     fact makes answerable, deduplicated                               128
;   and every case has an answering row, so this is not a wall of
;     agreeing zeros                                                    256
;   and more than ten are MULTI-MATCH — the only cases that test
;     first-match order at all                                          512
;
;   THE CHECK NOBODY AUTHORED: summing a count shape over every distinct
;     key for a relation equals the number of facts carrying it. A
;     property of counting, true of any correct implementation. A
;     swapped column leaves every single answer plausible and breaks
;     this sum — the one failure the sweep cannot see, because a
;     swapped column would be swapped in the reference too            1024
;
;   A PAGE OF CODE, measured on the emitted text:
;   python over 50 lines                                              2048
;   javascript over 50 lines                                          4096
;   go over 50 lines                                                  8192
;   and Form under 20 — it carries no `slet` row, so it cannot spell
;     the statement page, and the refusal is the absence of a row
;     rather than a branch in the harness                             16384
;
;   THE DELTA WITNESS: no single output can prove it was generated rather
;     than typed. What a template cannot do is track a predicted change in
;     its input. Add one fact and exactly one count answer rises by
;     exactly one                                                       32768
;   while 104 of the other 105 stay identical — not 105, because the
;     injected row has subject == object, so the object-column count for
